<resources>
    <!-- Six-inch F4 (2026-10-26): from a 720 dp tall screen the glance row's text takes two lines, so a short message
         shows whole. 720 dp is where the compact music tile and three two-line rows still fit the page's scroller at
         font scale 1.3 with 3-button navigation and a 48 dp status bar (LockGlanceLayoutTest); the Jelly Star's
         569 dp stays one line. The qualifier reads Configuration.screenHeightDp: with targetSdk 36 on Android 15+ the
         whole window, system bars included (what the 720 - 48 - 48 derivation assumes); on Android 14 the height less
         both bars, so there two lines need about 816 dp of screen - stricter, the fit still holds. -->
    <integer name="glance_row_text_lines">2</integer>
</resources>
